  "heading": "\\real.cauchy.relation",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Cauchy-sequence equivalence}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\real.cauchy.relation]\nDefines: E is \\equivalence.relation:on{\\rational.cauchy.sequences}\nexpresses:\n. forAll: A ::= a(n_) ::= qa_ is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\n  then:\n  . forAll: B ::= b(n_) ::= qb_ is \\cauchy.rational.sequence\n    then:\n    . have: E(A, B)\n      iff:\n      . forAll: epsilon is \\rational\n        where: \\rational.zero \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\n        then:\n        . exists: N is \\natural\n          suchThat:\n          . forAll: n is \\natural\n            where: N \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n            then: \\rational.abs(a(n) \\.rational.-./ b(n)) \\:rational.less?:/ epsilon\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Cauchy-sequence equivalence\"\n. description: \"Two rational Cauchy sequences are equivalent when their termwise\n                difference converges to zero.\"\nId: \"24cd9c1f-5185-495b-8107-e9cce4d5dc76\"",
